# Closing Module

> Coordinate, approve, and complete mineral acquisition transactions from title approval through final funding.

---

# Overview

The Closing module manages the final phase of the mineral acquisition lifecycle.

Once Title Review and Curative requirements have been completed, the Closing module coordinates document verification, settlement preparation, payment authorization, and final acquisition recording.

The module provides a standardized closing process, ensuring every transaction is legally complete, financially approved, and fully documented before ownership is transferred.

---

# Objectives

The Closing module enables users to:

- Coordinate acquisition closings
- Verify closing readiness
- Assemble closing packages
- Track closing progress
- Manage settlement approvals
- Authorize payments
- Complete acquisitions
- Maintain a complete audit trail

---

# Key Features

## Closing Management

Each Closing Record contains:

- Closing Number
- Deal
- Owner
- Asset
- Closing Coordinator
- Scheduled Closing Date
- Closing Status
- Settlement Amount
- Funding Status
- Notes

---

## Closing Checklist

Every closing follows a standardized checklist.

### Required Items

- Executed Purchase & Sale Agreement
- Approved Title Review
- Completed Curative
- Verified Ownership
- Closing Statement
- Wire Instructions / Mailing Address
- Payment Approval
- Signed Closing Documents

Closing cannot proceed until all required items are complete.

---

## Closing Statuses

- Pending
- Ready for Closing
- Scheduled
- Awaiting Funding
- Closed
- Cancelled

---

## Settlement Information

Each Closing tracks:

- Purchase Price
- Adjustments
- Taxes
- Fees
- Net Payment
- Funding Method
- Payment Reference

